A||N||1||BlueMagnolia||Interchanges||||5||
Z||000000||BlueMagnolia||01-18-2000||06:08 PM||||I am replacing my 4 cylinder engine in my<BR>'84 Fiero, The engine that the guy is selling me came oout of a '84 Omega,they are suppose to interchange, but what are the differences in the motors? Will I have make special modifications for this engine?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||01-18-2000||06:43 PM||||I put a 2.5 4 cyl from an 83 Phoenix into an 84 Fiero. The motor itself should be the same. You shouldn't have to modify anything although you may need to swap some things from the Fiero motor. Some things you will probably need from the Fiero (at least I did):<P>- Wiring harness<BR>- Temp guage sensor (if omega just had an idiot light)<BR>- Throttle cable bracket <BR>- Radiator/heater hose outlet on water pump<BR>- Heater hose tube under intake manifold (or bend as I did)<BR>- Some other misc. brackets, wire clamps, etc.<P>Look at everything CAREFULLY... Some things may be similar but slightly different. I missed the Throttle Cable bracket at first because they looked very similar. They were made a little different and when I hooked the Fiero throttle cable to the Phoenix bracket the throttle would only close half way. Swapped brackets and everything was fine, but would have been easier out of the car (plus it wouldn't have mysteriously idled at 3000-4000 the first start  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>DON'T get rid of ANYTHING that came out of the Fiero until you are completely done.<P>Good Luck.||||reg||1
